WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.665
FedRAMP High is a baseline for cloud services supporting high-impact federal use cases

00:00:04.665 --> 00:00:08.220
where security failures could have severe or catastrophic adverse effects.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.690
It connects impact categorization to stronger security expectations,

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:15.355
engineering implementation, assessment evidence, authorization support,

00:00:15.355 --> 00:00:16.600
and continuous monitoring.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.490
High is demanding because the mission and data risk are demanding.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.810
The most important ideas are impact, scope, responsibility, evidence, resilience,

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:24.710
and operations.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.360
Impact explains why High is appropriate.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.600
Scope defines the cloud service offering and its dependencies.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.945
Responsibility clarifies what the provider, customer, platform,

00:00:32.945 --> 00:00:34.800
and inherited services handle.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.660
Evidence supports assessment conclusions.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.530
Resilience and operations show whether the service can sustain its security posture over

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:40.920
time.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.425
Success depends on disciplined engineering and honest documentation.

00:00:44.425 --> 00:00:49.460
Strong identity controls, privileged access management, segmentation, logging, monitoring,

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.105
vulnerability management, change control, recovery planning,

00:00:52.105 --> 00:00:54.320
and secure development practices all matter.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.560
Documentation must match the live system.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.425
Inherited controls must be traceable.

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.520
Customer responsibilities must be clear.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:03.190
Unsupported claims are not enough for high-impact risk.

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:06.210
The goal is not simply to pass a review or claim a stronger label.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:10.470
The goal is to help federal stakeholders make informed risk decisions about high-impact

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.405
cloud services.

00:01:11.405 --> 00:01:15.560
A strong High program gives those stakeholders a credible picture of the system boundary,

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.020
control implementation, evidence, known risks, remediation work, resilience posture,

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.760
and continuing monitoring discipline.
